{"record_type":"method","qualified_name":"github.com/livekit/livekit-server/pkg/config.Config.ToCLIFlagNames","decl":"func (conf *Config) ToCLIFlagNames(existingFlags []cli.Flag) map[string]reflect.Value","span":{"start_line":558,"end_line":606},"summary":"Builds a map from generated CLI flag names to reflected config fields, excluding existing flag names and traversing nested YAML-tagged structs.","summary_step":["1. Collects names from existing CLI flags so generated flags do not collide.","2. Starts breadth-first traversal at the Config value with an empty tag prefix.","3. Reads yaml tags, detects inline fields, skips empty or ignored tags, and builds dot-separated YAML paths.","4. Skips paths that already exist as CLI flags.","5. Enqueues nested struct values for traversal and records non-struct values as generated flag targets.","6. Returns the generated flag name to reflected value map."]}
{"record_type":"method","qualified_name":"github.com/livekit/livekit-server/pkg/config.Config.ValidateKeys","decl":"func (conf *Config) ValidateKeys() error","span":{"start_line":608,"end_line":643},"summary":"Validates API key configuration by loading key files, checking file permissions, requiring at least one key, and warning about short production secrets.","summary_step":["1. If KeyFile is set, checks that other-user permissions are zero and opens the file.","2. Decodes YAML key data into conf.Keys and closes the file when done.","3. Returns ErrKeysNotSet when no keys are configured.","4. In non-development mode, logs warnings for secrets shorter than 32 characters.","5. Returns nil when key configuration is usable."]}
{"record_type":"func","qualified_name":"github.com/livekit/livekit-server/pkg/config.GenerateCLIFlags","decl":"func GenerateCLIFlags(existingFlags []cli.Flag, hidden bool) ([]cli.Flag, error)","span":{"start_line":645,"end_line":740},"summary":"Generates urfave CLI flags from default configuration fields and environment variable names based on YAML paths.","summary_step":["1. Uses DefaultConfig.ToCLIFlagNames to discover reflected config fields that are not already represented by base flags.","2. Resolves pointer field kinds through their element kind.","3. Builds LIVEKIT-prefixed environment variable names from dot-separated config paths.","4. Creates the matching cli.Flag type for supported bool, string, integer, unsigned integer, and floating kinds.","5. Skips slice, map, and struct fields that are not directly representable as generated flags.","6. Returns an error for unsupported generated field kinds and otherwise returns the generated flag slice."]}
